[Music]  hi everyone and welcome to in two  minutes apologies for missing last week  I kind of wrecked my voice because I was  doing the Batman where is she voice  around the office a little bit too much  and I only started doing it because I  finally got to play some of Arkham  Knight and I've got to say it is shaping  up quite nicely it's if it's really fine  balance of being both quite familiar in  terms of its gameplay but it also adds  in a lot of new stuff that's making it  really fun to play so I thought I'd do  this week's episode all about the new  things we can expect in Batman Arkham  Knight and I promise to never do that  voice again ever  Batman didn't become the world's  greatest detective with just a  deerstalker and a magnifying glass a  smaller much appreciated addition to  Arkham Knight is that all of bats  high-tech kit is now a neatly organized  in a gadget wheel yes that means no more  fiddling around with the d-pad to find  the right piece of equipment in fact  missions are organized in much the same  way meaning that you won't be missing  out on anything that the huge Gotham has  to offer  we've played as Catwoman Nightwing and  Robin before but always in their own  self-contained missions now you can  switch between being the bat the cat the  Christmas bird and Nightwing made fight  with a mechanic called dual play which  is basically like playing co-op but with  yourself I found that it switched up  combat quite nicely because you can go  from Batman speedy but measured hits to  Nightwing's frenetic acrobatics with  just the push of a button or you can  slow things right down another new  mechanic is the Fiat takedown which is  similar to the breach mechanic from Call  of Duty highlight the goons that you  want to surprise and delete at the first  one after contact time will slow and you  can aim at the next attack them all and  they fall like dominoes you can upgrade  this ability with Wayne tech points to  take down yet more enemies and while  we've not seen any traditional predator  rooms in Arkham Knight just yet the Fiat  takedown is a nice nod to the  claustrophobic and stealthy gameplay of  the first game and obviously I was gonna  mention the Batmobile it's had a bit of  an overhaul since we last saw it on the  lawn of Arkham Asylum I'll be honest I  expected it to be quite sluggish given  that it's a big hulking tank  in reality it's quite zippy in pursuit  mode it punches through the environment  hammers round corners and boosts over  gaps with ease it feels like it's got  some weight to it but it's also quite  easy to control when you take it out on  Riddler's racetracks or chase fools down  the streets of Gotham things can get a  little fast and furious so if you need  extra control you can easily pop it into  battle mode which changes how it  controls and makes it more tanky and  while nothing will ever really beat the  feeling of jumping and gliding off the  top of Gotham's most famous buildings  the Batmobile is still a pretty nice way  of getting around town if you want to  see more from the Caped Crusader make  your way to GameSpot comm we have a  bunch of videos and articles all about  the world's greatest detective in the  meantime you can catch me Joe chillin on  Twitter at Lucy James games I'll see you  next time  just gonna get rid of the phlegm come on  a great day awesome one day I'll say  Twitter love today oh that's it

